▶ UEP IoT/M2M hardening
  ✔ authenticates machine telemetry with Ed25519 (a registered machine key is mandatory) (18.507533ms)
  ✔ rejects unsigned telemetry and telemetry signed by another key (UEP-B13) (14.334248ms)
  ✔ rejects replayed nonces even under a new sequence (14.799584ms)
  ✔ uses deterministic CBOR for the telemetry payload and exposes clear next actions (19.875059ms)
  ✔ enforces the tighter future timestamp window (14.66828ms)
✔ UEP IoT/M2M hardening (82.75219ms)
▶ IoT settlement is based on verified telemetry
  ✔ normal settle of an IoT order is blocked without verified telemetry (also via the marketplace) (30.925665ms)
  ✔ verification only accepts the report delivered to the order (15.64656ms)
  ✔ a usage shortfall blocks release; the arbiter splits by verified units and value is conserved (22.641863ms)
  ✔ units above the contracted quantity are rejected (11.211357ms)
✔ IoT settlement is based on verified telemetry (80.78785ms)
▶ IoT authorization hardening
  ✔ requires an authenticated buyer, provider (after the window) or arbiter to settle (19.984003ms)
  ✔ providers and machines are registered with the provider's signature (8.733105ms)
  ✔ requires the admin signature to deactivate a provider; the provider may deactivate its machine (23.778056ms)
  ✔ IoT hold funds the remainder after the locked reservation deposit (17.536875ms)
  ✔ IoT requests are fail-closed: unregistered or wrongly signed buyers cannot reserve (7.967667ms)
✔ IoT authorization hardening (78.43377ms)
